# Registry block media (images & video)

Use this when a block needs bundled raster images (PNG, JPG, WebP) or video (MP4, WebM). Most blocks (navbars, SVG-only sections, etc.) do not need this.

## Consumer install (shadcn add)

`shadcn build` + `post-registry-build.mjs` strip binary `content` from `public/r/*.json` and set `meta.installUrl`. **The shadcn CLI skips `registry:file` entries with no `content`**, so images/video are not created by `shadcn add` alone.

After `pnpm registry:build`, consumers must also fetch media — use the copy command from the block toolbar (`shadcn add` plus `curl` lines). Tests in `registry-shadcn-media-install.test.ts` guard this.

## Where assets live

**Images**

```
public/images/blocks/<block-id>/
  hero-section-v8-bg.png
  avatar_1.png
```

**Video**

```
public/videos/blocks/<block-id>/
  screen-demo.mp4
```
